n='tcp-flow-control'
edit(n,"If the sender just blasted bytes, the receiver's kernel buffer would fill and everything after that would be dropped, then retransmitted, then dropped again.","Without receiver flow control, sustained arrivals faster than the application drains them can exhaust finite receive buffering and cause drops. Retransmitting does not remove that bottleneck.","Scope overflow to sustained excess arrival and avoid a universal drop/retransmit cycle.",rfc(9293))
edit(n,'As the application calls `recv()`, the buffer drains and the receiver advertises a bigger window. If the application stops reading, the window shrinks to zero and the sender must stop.','As the application calls `recv()`, the buffer drains and window-update policy can permit a larger advertised window. If the application stops reading while data continues to arrive, finite receive capacity can be exhausted: the receiver advertises zero and the sender must stop ordinary new-data transmission.','Window updates are policy-dependent; a stopped reader alone does not imply immediate zero window.',rfc(9293))
edit(n,'every window update can move the right edge.','An accepted window update can change the right edge.','Invalid or stale advertisements need not update sender state.',rfc(9293))
edit(n,'The window can only be as large as the receive buffer.','The advertised window must be supported by the receiver’s capacity and update policy; it is not a direct byte-for-byte reading of allocated socket memory.','Avoid equating sequence-space advertisement with memory allocation.',rfc(9293))
edit(n,'was written for Telnet, where every keystroke became a 41-byte packet carrying 1 byte of data.','addresses, among other cases, interactive terminal traffic where a one-byte keystroke could occupy a 41-byte IPv4/TCP packet with minimal headers.','RFC 896 describes a possible interactive small-packet case, not a property of every Telnet keystroke.',rfc(896))
edit(n,'the sender keeps in-flight data within min(rwnd, cwnd).','ordinary new-data sending is constrained by both rwnd and cwnd; shrinkage, recovery and probes need additional rules.','Already-in-flight data need not instantly fall below a newly reduced window.',rfc(9293)+rfc(5681))
edit(n,'Throughput is capped at window / RTT.','In the fixed-window steady-state model, throughput is capped at window / RTT.','Carry the model assumptions into the summary.',rfc(7323))
edit(n,"A zero window stops the sender; the persist timer's probes stop a lost window update causing deadlock.","A zero window stops ordinary new-data transmission; successfully delivered persist probes and replies can recover from a lost window update.","Probes do not guarantee progress through persistent loss or endpoint failure.",rfc(9293))
edit(n,'Nagle (sender) and delayed ACK (receiver) together stall write-write-read patterns by the delayed-ACK timeout.','Nagle (sender) and delayed ACK (receiver) can stall a split write-write-read exchange until the delayed-ACK timer expires.','Not every pair of writes produces the required packet/ACK timing.',rfc(1122))
qedit(n,2,'workedExample','1. The receiver advertises an acceptable sequence range, reflecting buffering and update policy rather than exactly reporting free memory.\n2. In the simplified ordinary new-data model, the remaining budget is `max(0, min(rwnd, cwnd) - flight)`.\n3. rwnd provides receiver flow control; cwnd controls network congestion. Recovery, probes and window shrinkage require additional rules.','Align worked explanation with corrected sequence-space definition.',rfc(9293)+rfc(5681))
qedit(n,3,'options.2.explanation','A small cwnd can coexist with a zero receive window, but it does not explain the independently observed blocked receiving thread and full receive queue.','Do not treat independently controlled windows as mutually exclusive.',rfc(9293))
qedit(n,9,'options.2.explanation','Full-sized ready segments are not held by Nagle’s small-segment rule, although partial tails and incremental writes can be affected. The supplied captures establish the window-scaling problem in this scenario.','Bulk transfer does not guarantee all application writes produce full segments.',rfc(1122))
qreplace(n,11,'prompt','rwnd = 256 KB (262,144 bytes)','rwnd = 256 KiB (262,144 bytes)','Correct binary unit notation.')
